# Joint PoN source, clock and resource evidence — 2026-11-09

**HOLD / NO-GO.** This package records concrete implementation fixes and their
fixed-source observations. All-legal-algorithm resource cost, joint classical/
quantum time–difficulty–credit security, and honest service under the original
public resource contract remain unqualified.

## Source and implementation

| Role | Commit |
| --- | --- |
| Complete #821 base | `e798d7125724d4b9f98c24d00cc80031f2eab4a9` |
| Initial implementation, with separate outcomes | `fc5c44ca91c56e77ca2ffc9943e10f0f777a5937` |
| Corrected tested implementation | `11791e2da79b69322271be2cffe03725165151d1` |
| Its hosted prospective merge | `b472c21f7b14ba27bb87d9d2f52d299365ed3145` |

The tested tree is `162552848110fda532504b78865a16930bc6d9bb`, containing
26,124 tracked entries / 2,485,379,627 bytes. Fixed-source recorder commands retain
individual source-before/source-after checks, full output, exit status and byte
hashes. The V4 observation pair retains one full-source check before and after
the pair, with separate executable, output and process receipts for each child.
Earlier capture gaps are listed below.
[Draft PR #827](https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain/pull/827)
targets #821. An evidence publication child has its own source checks and does
not inherit these native execution identities. The desktop bare repository is
only object transport; tests use complete checkouts.

The [joint contract](../../docs/research/PON_JOINT_RESOURCE_CONTRACT_20261108.md)
and [V4 contract](../../docs/research/PON_W1_LIFECYCLE_COST_V4.md) give the full
scope. History rechecks the same deadline after a successful mandatory Host
callback, preserving the callback error and durable work. Public PGH2 uses a
fresh-clock observed-ancestry activation for new and duplicate packets. Its
original fully charged noncancellable tail remains, and the added walk is
O(history depth). V4 flushes lifecycle boundaries, keeps unfinished cost unknown,
and requires both complete native verifiers before counting verified work.
No observation adds chain credit. These changes do not guarantee every later
scheduling boundary or a throughput improvement.

