## V4 native observations

The 13-arm / 9-material / 8-sample roster retains all 936 cohorts, including
unsupported combinations: 23,069 records, 1,888 searches, 3,848 completed
generation attempts, 3,776 full verifier calls and 288 canonical candidate
records. Process/reader both exit 0; all credit increments are zero. A separate
real SIGTERM child exits -15; its reader exits 3 with INCOMPLETE, nine records,
zero completed attempts and unfinished_resource_cost=null. The child consumes
nonzero user CPU. No claim locates the signal inside a proof instruction.

The loaded/before/after executable hash is
`bd74dea5a8b1ddc57e86f1d181c3cdb287321dc0b9651e03b6f21adfcfe2f45a`;
compressed binary bytes are retained. The two implementation runs match over
all records after excluding only three documented timing fields. This transfers
no source or resource qualification. The diagnostic target is 1/2, not MU1's
1/16; its sixteen classical/quantum resource points remain unknown. Nested
timing scopes cannot be added, and these runs do not use the public quota.

## Actual hosted outcomes

### Original three-run native campaign

[Run 42553751914](https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain/actions/runs/42553751914)
actually builds and executes all three planned release campaigns on 117.
Build exits 0; each original campaign exits 101 with a valid retained report.
There are no phase startup errors, report-validation failures or finalization
failures. Complete campaigns meeting the original criteria: **0/3**.

This original campaign uses three 30-second modes per run. Its per-run outcomes
are identical across the three runs:

| Mode in each run | Hostile processes | Planned confirmation rounds | Observed rounds | Confirmed rounds | Unobserved rounds | Submit ACKs |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| baseline | 0 | 3 | 2 | 1 | 1 | 14/14 |
| from-zero | 24 | 3 | 1 | 0 | 2 | 7/7 |
| late-product | 24 | 3 | 1 | 0 | 2 | 7/7 |

Across nine phases: **27 planned, 12 observed, 3 confirmed, 15 unobserved**.
An unobserved round is not a completed failed execution and has no zero-cost
assumption. All nine phases retain `PUBLIC_REQUEST_DEADLINE`,
`receiver_client_state_equal=false` and
`genuine_budget_depletion_observed=false`. The original finite criteria remain
false. The attack-free mode has partial confirmation and still fails its full
original target.

The controller/build domain retains its declared 4-CPU / 16-GiB limit, while
the actual receiver/verifier phase retains the original 0.25-CPU / 2-GiB public
domain. These domains are not conflated. The checked original test binary is
12,601,856 bytes, before/after SHA-256
`f9cd85c7b053746cea0610aa184bd4993def306bd6bb8aeb875583c803dfa619`.
The complete original provider ZIP, including that binary, is retained.

### Original four-second service cases

These are separate cases from the 30-second, three-run campaign.
[Required-baseline run 42553751938](https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain/actions/runs/42553751938)
has the following four completed native failures:

| Completed job | Native child calls | Baseline independent confirmation | Pressure independent confirmation |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Protocol head, 128954796906 | 5/5 exit 0; no timeout | 1/1 | 0/1 |
| Protocol prospective merge, 128954797047 | 5/5 exit 0; no timeout | 1/1 | 0/1 |
| Cross-architecture x64, 128954796813 | 5/5 exit 0; no timeout | 1/1 | 0/1 |
| Cross-architecture arm64, 128954796735 | 5/5 exit 0; no timeout | 1/1 | 0/1 |

Each keeps the original four-second / 16-hostile case, actual
`cpu.max=25000 100000`, 2 GiB, zero swap and 256 PIDs. OOM and OOM-kill counts
are zero. Service and sustained reports pass, but the confirmation validator
rejects `CONFIRMATION_TARGET`; its later predicates are not independently
claimed as passed. The execution-completed flag only records that child calls
returned. Acceptance remains false.

All four pressure cases retain 7/7 Submit ACKs for blocks carrying one business
item. Head, prospective merge and x64 fail the last independent replay with
`PUBLIC_REQUEST_DEADLINE`. ARM64 finishes its six observed replays, but the
seventh History response fails or misses the original window.

The changed History control is on this actual replay path. No paired causal
experiment attributes these failures to the change or excludes its involvement.
The new V4 example command is not reached after the failing from-zero command;
the Growth-specific branch is not used by this ordinary Submit/History fixture.

