## Preserved failures and capture limits

The original-source History comparison uses unchanged e798 production plus
only five added controls: 8/10 pass and 2 fail; all five historical controls pass.
The failed owner test reaches its exclusive branch and stops, so the old-source
shared branch does not run. Its initial loader environment reports the unchanged
SQLite fence as UNQUALIFIED. This component comparison does not qualify SQLite
or the public Host. The saved qualified-retry script was not executed.

Two fc5 libtest builds end with rustc SIGKILL, with two then one Cargo build job;
the cause is not uniquely established. Neither failed build is authority to run
a stale corrected-source test executable. The first strict Clippy reports two
shared-wrapper dead-code sites and one indexed loop; 117 fixes those sites.
Its first Clippy then fails ENOSPC. Only this task's reproducible cache and
archived duplicate comparison worktree are removed; the same source and strict
command pass on retry. Each failed command receipt remains separate.

The preliminary uncommitted CI-placement run records 85 failures and 14 errors
among 165 cases. Its console was truncated without full redirection. Surviving
source, counts and an explicit capture-gap note are retained; missing complete
output is not reconstructed. Original prefix/from-zero guards remain intact
when the new command is placed after their mandatory prefix.

Remote preparation retains a one-newline transfer-SHA rejection before any
build or test. A default-thread wrapper is explicitly stopped during --no-run;
its recorder completes the build, and the wrapper exits -15 before tests. Serial
execution is a separate run. Serial-02 passes History/Public and then fails its
own narrow roster expectation: store::growth::tests:: contains 74 names and its
sibling difference_tests:: contains five more. Remaining-03 executes the full
79-name store::growth:: scope and the remaining Consensus/DAA suites. The two
original ignored experiments and the process-cut child's expected exit 91
remain. Serial-02's overall FAIL is not rewritten.

Git transport missing-base-blob failures and the existing gh CLI's projectCards
deprecation are retained as publication observations. Exact base Git objects
and a normal body-only REST update use the same authenticated ProfHepta channel.
No force push, merge, permission bypass or production activation is performed.
The first hosted readback selector accidentally included resource files in its
source-file set and stopped before issuing a summary; the corrected selector
checks the actual matching source-before/source-after records. Original native
bytes were unchanged. A local 1-MiB base64 transport probe was truncated and
was never transferred; the verified 512-KiB size is used instead.

